Source diving would be required in order to be certain,
and I can't at the moment seem to find the bit of code
that handles poison when a thrown object hits the player.

In general, however, luck has an effect on a fair
variety of different phenomena in the game. 

When the numbers involved are small (a single -1 luck 
penalty, for example) you are usually unlikely to notice, 
unless it puts you on the other side of a critical 
threshhold for something important (typically, prayer
or wishing).  Having a *large* luck penalty, however, 
can make a somewhat larger difference than you might
expect.  Dangerous events normally considered unlikely 
can become commonplace.  Just for example, it is
inadvisable to try to unlock or loot a chest if you 
have large negative luck.

